<main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
        <h1 class="fade-up fade-up-2">Parachute Vault <span class="alpha-tag">alpha</span></h1>
        <p class="tagline fade-up fade-up-3">An open memory layer for your AIs</p>
        <p class="subtitle fade-up fade-up-4">Your AI's memory is fragmented. Claude Code doesn't know what Claude Chats know. Claude Cowork doesn't know what Claude Code is working on. Across ChatGPT, Gemini, every tool — each a walled garden.</p>

        <div class="hero-install fade-up fade-up-5">
            <div class="code-inline">
                <code>bun add -g @openparachute/cli &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
            </div>
            <p class="install-note">One open knowledge graph — notes, tags, links — that every AI you use can read and write to. On your machine, over <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank">MCP</a>. Requires <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank">Bun</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Use it immediately -->
    <section class="section fade-up fade-up-6">
        <h2>Use it immediately</h2>
        <p>Run that install inside any Claude Code session — Claude Code picks up the MCP automatically and can read and write your Vault before you leave the terminal.</p>
        <p>Want it elsewhere? One more command:</p>
        <div class="code-inline" style="margin: 1rem 0;">
            <code>parachute expose tailnet</code>
        </div>
        <p>Now your Vault is reachable at an HTTPS URL on your tailnet. Point Claude Desktop at it. Point ChatGPT Desktop at it. Point Claude Cowork, Gemini, your own custom agent — anything that speaks MCP — at the same URL. They all read and write to the same graph.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- What this unlocks -->
    <section class="section">
        <h2>What this unlocks</h2>
        <p><strong>Persistent memory across every AI you use.</strong> Notes your Claude Code session wrote are there for ChatGPT to read an hour later. What you capture on your phone becomes context for the next chat you open on your laptop.</p>
        <p><strong>A compounding knowledge graph.</strong> As your AIs read and write, the graph grows. Wikilinks resolve, tags accrete, notes point at each other. Queries get richer over time — not because the index is bigger, but because what's there gets more useful.</p>
        <p><strong>Your data, your hardware.</strong> It's a SQLite file on your disk. If we disappeared tomorrow, your graph is still there — portable, exportable, entirely yours.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Security -->
    <section class="section">
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>Default install is loopback-only — nothing on the network until you ask. <code>parachute expose tailnet</code> keeps traffic on your tailnet. <code>parachute expose public</code> adds Tailscale Funnel for public HTTPS and strongly recommends <strong>OAuth + 2FA</strong> on the Vault.</p>
        <p>API tokens are available for programmatic access — useful for your own agents, scripts, or services you want to pin tightly. Per-token scoping (read-only, write-only, per-resource) is coming next.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Optional UI -->
    <section class="section">
        <h2>Want a UI?</h2>
        <p>We've built <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-notes" target="_blank"><strong>Parachute Notes</strong></a> — an alpha-quality PWA you can install or fork. It's an example front-end, not the definitive UI. Browse, edit, capture voice memos, install on your phone. <code>parachute install notes</code>. Build your own if you prefer; the API is open.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Principles -->
    <section class="section">
        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Local-first.</strong> Your data is a SQLite file on your disk.</li>
            <li><strong>Open standard.</strong> Built on <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank">MCP</a>. Whatever AI you use today or next year, it works with Parachute.</li>
            <li><strong>Open source, AGPL.</strong> Read every line of code that touches your notes.</li>
            <li><strong>Extensible.</strong> The service contracts are small and stable. Plug in your own modules.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta">
        <h2>Install in one line</h2>
        <div class="code-inline" style="margin: 1.5rem auto; max-width: 640px;">
            <code>bun add -g @openparachute/cli &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
